@startuml SSD-S3-allocate-stock
' System sequence diagram for UC-05 Allocate stock to orders and UC-09 Trace item, slice S3
' Black-box view: actors, the system as a single lifeline, system events and returned outcomes only
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

title SSD-S3 Allocate stock (UC-05) and Trace item (UC-09)

actor "Hub staff member" as A
actor "Traceability coordinator\n(STAFF role)" as T
participant ":KerryHubSystem" as S

== UC-05 Allocate stock to orders ==

A -> S : viewOrderForAllocation(orderId)
alt order found and actor permitted
  S --> A : OrderAllocationView (per line: product, requested,\n allocated so far, available)
else actor is a volunteer (1a)
  S --> A : Failure(NOT_PERMITTED)
else order does not exist (1b)
  S --> A : Failure(NOT_FOUND)
end

loop for each order line to allocate
  A -> S : allocateOrderLine(orderLineId)
  alt valid and permitted
    S --> A : LineAllocationResult (per lot used: producer, batch,\n quantity; total allocated; shortfall)
  else actor is a volunteer (1a)
    S --> A : Failure(NOT_PERMITTED)
  else order line does not exist
    S --> A : Failure(NOT_FOUND)
  else line already fully allocated (3a)
    S --> A : Failure(INVALID_STATE)
  end
end

note over A, S
  A shortfall is not a failure: the result shows it (4a)
  and UC-06 Handle shortfall continues (S4, «extend»).
  viewOrderForAllocation only reads data, so it has no contract.
  allocateOrderLine changes state: contract OC-06.
end note

== UC-09 Trace item ==

T -> S : traceOrderLine(orderId, productId)
alt found and actor permitted
  S --> T : TraceView (per allocation: producer, batch or batch missing,\n harvest and use-by dates, delivery date, quantity)
else actor is a volunteer (1a)
  S --> T : Failure(NOT_PERMITTED)
else order, or a line for that product, does not exist (1b)
  S --> T : Failure(NOT_FOUND)
end

note over T, S
  traceOrderLine only reads data, so it has no contract.
  An empty trace (nothing allocated yet, 2a) is a success.
end note
@enduml